    {
      "title": "Gather your existing bill and additional evidence",
      "detail": "You already have the purchase bill for the Rs. 3,000 mixer bought on 1 October 2026. You still need to gather the warranty card, photos or videos showing the defect, and copies of your written communications with HomeMart. Note down the exact dates when you asked for a refund and when HomeMart refused it, as those missing details are important for your claim."
    },
    {
      "title": "Send a formal written complaint to HomeMart",
      "detail": "Write to HomeMart stating that the mixer has a defect [SRC:CPA2019-S2-10] and request a full refund of Rs. 3,000. Refusing to refund money for defective goods within the specified receipt period or 30 days may be considered an unfair trade practice [SRC:CPA2019-S2-47-viii]. Keep a copy of your letter or email as evidence."
    },
    {
      "title": "Report the issue to the National Consumer Helpline",
      "detail": "If HomeMart does not resolve the matter, you can register a grievance with the National Consumer Helpline [SRC:NCH-CONTACT]. You can call toll-free on 1915 or 1800114000 (8 AM to 8 PM), send a WhatsApp message to +918800001915, or file a complaint online at consumerhelpline.gov.in [SRC:NCH-CONTACT]."
    },
    {
      "title": "File a consumer complaint on e-Jagriti",
      "detail": "If the dispute remains unresolved, you may file a formal complaint with the District Consumer Commission electronically through e-jagriti.gov.in [SRC:CPA2019-S35-1]. Since your dispute value is Rs. 3,000, which is up to Rs. 5 lakh, the filing fee is Nil [SRC:CDRC2023-R7-FEE]. Ensure you file the complaint within two years from the date the issue arose [SRC:CPA2019-S69], and include the required documents such as a list of dates, memo of parties, and notarised affidavit [SRC:EJAGRITI-LIMITATION-DOCS]."
    }
  ]
}

